1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:00,910
The US government

2
00:00:00,910 --> 00:00:02,030
just doubled how much

3
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:03,070
of its own long-term

4
00:00:03,070 --> 00:00:03,780
debt it plans to

5
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:04,260
buy back.

6
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:05,080
And that is a pretty

7
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:06,300
extraordinary sentence.

8
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,300
So here's what happened.

9
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,210
Long-term US borrowing

10
00:00:08,210 --> 00:00:09,300
costs have been surging.

11
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:10,550
The 30-year Treasury

12
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:11,150
yield just hit

13
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:12,240
its highest level since

14
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,550
2007, as investors are

15
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:14,540
worrying about inflation

16
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:15,350
and as national debt

17
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:16,350
has crossed over $40

18
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:16,980
trillion.

19
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:17,570
So the Treasury

20
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:18,000
stepped in.

21
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:18,610
It announced

22
00:00:18,610 --> 00:00:19,300
that it will double

23
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,370
its buybacks for certain

24
00:00:20,370 --> 00:00:21,240
10- to 30-year

25
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:22,180
government bonds,

26
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:22,930
from $2 billion

27
00:00:22,930 --> 00:00:23,930
to at least $4 billion

28
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:24,740
per operation.

29
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:25,330
Basically,

30
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:26,130
the government issues

31
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:26,820
Treasury bonds to

32
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:27,500
borrow money.

33
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:28,160
Those bonds trade

34
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:28,910
on the open market,

35
00:00:28,910 --> 00:00:29,670
and now the Treasury

36
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:30,520
is increasing how much

37
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:31,680
of that existing debt

38
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:32,540
it can buy back,

39
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:32,940
with the goal

40
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:33,720
of improving liquidity

41
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:34,300
and taking off

42
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:35,090
some pressure off

43
00:00:35,090 --> 00:00:35,880
the long end of the

44
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:36,600
bond market.

45
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,730
This is not quantitative

46
00:00:37,730 --> 00:00:38,845
easing, and it is not

47
00:00:38,845 --> 00:00:39,900
yield curve control.

48
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:40,700
This is the Treasury

49
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:41,750
managing the composition

50
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:42,600
of government debt,

51
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:43,160
and the timing

52
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:43,730
is what makes

53
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:44,520
this interesting.

54
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:45,260
The Treasury made

55
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:45,750
the surprise

56
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:46,880
announcement immediately

57
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:47,540
after long-term

58
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:48,670
borrowing costs reached

59
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:49,650
levels we haven't seen

60
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:50,800
in nearly two decades.

61
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,050
And the market reacted

62
00:00:52,050 --> 00:00:52,780
instantly.

63
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:53,450
Long-term yields

64
00:00:53,450 --> 00:00:54,400
dropped, and the dollar

65
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,280
initially sold off.

66
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:56,120
So the bigger story

67
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:56,800
is that America

68
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:57,750
has more than $40

69
00:00:57,750 --> 00:00:58,720
trillion in debt.

70
00:00:58,720 --> 00:00:59,480
Long-term borrowing

71
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,230
costs are climbing,

72
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:00,810
and the Treasury

73
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:01,740
is becoming increasingly

74
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:02,690
willing to intervene

75
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:03,350
in the bond market

76
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:03,700
to relieve

77
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:04,460
that pressure.

78
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:05,080
And the Treasury

79
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:05,790
Secretary has said

80
00:01:05,790 --> 00:01:06,540
that these buybacks

81
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:07,540
could even get bigger.

